{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1744782,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":"blue_un","paid":0,"title":"Quiz Nova","festival_id":504454,"organization_id":675999,"web_url":null,"start_date":"2026-09-02T18:31:00+05:30","end_date":"2026-10-16T16:45:00+05:30","location":null,"type":"quizzes","public_url":"quiz\/quiz-nova-techfest26-annual-technical-festival-of-sliet-sant-longowal-institute-of-engineering-and-technology-longo-1744782","region":"offline","details":"<p><strong>QUIZ-NOVA | techFEST'26<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>Opportunity Description:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>QUIZ-NOVA is an intellectually stimulating written quiz competition organized under the <strong>Atomheimer <\/strong>Domain by the <strong>Science Department<\/strong> as part of techFEST'26 at <strong>SLIET<\/strong>. The event aims to evaluate participants' knowledge, analytical thinking, logical reasoning, observation skills, and problem-solving abilities through a carefully designed assessment covering science, technology, and general aptitude.<\/p>\n<p>Participants will compete individually in a time-bound written quiz and will be ranked based on their performance, accuracy, and time efficiency.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Eligibility;<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Open to all Diploma, Undergraduate (UG), and Postgraduate (PG) students.<\/li>\n<li>Students from any branch or discipline of recognized colleges and universities are eligible to participate.<\/li>\n<li>Participants must carry a valid college\/student ID card for verification during the event.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Competition Format:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Individual Participation.<\/li>\n<li>Written Quiz Competition.<\/li>\n<li>Duration: 45 Minutes.<\/li>\n<li>Medium: English.<\/li>\n<li>Total Questions:\n<ul>\n<li>20 Multiple Choice Questions (MCQs)<\/li>\n<li>5 Integer-Based Questions<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<li>No Negative Marking.<\/li>\n<li>Blank space will be provided on the question paper for calculations.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Syllabus:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>The quiz may include questions from:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Physics (Class X, XI &amp; XII Level)<\/li>\n<li>Chemistry (Class X, XI &amp; XII Level)<\/li>\n<li>Mathematics (Class X, XI &amp; XII Level)<\/li>\n<li>Logical and Analytical Reasoning<\/li>\n<li>Tech-Based General Knowledge<\/li>\n<li>Miscellaneous Topics<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Evaluation &amp; Ranking:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Participants will be evaluated using the following criteria:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Quiz Score<\/li>\n<li>Accuracy Percentage<\/li>\n<li>Time Score Percentage<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Ranking Formula:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Ranking Score = (0.7 &times; Quiz Score) + (0.2 &times; Accuracy %) + (0.1 &times; Time Score %)<\/p>\n<p>Where:<\/p>\n<p>Accuracy (%) = (Correct Answers &divide; Total Questions Attempted) &times; 100<\/p>\n<p>Time Score (%) = ((Maximum Time &minus; Time Taken) &divide; Maximum Time) &times; 100<\/p>\n<p><strong>Rewards &amp; Recognition:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Exciting prizes for the Top 3 Winners.<\/li>\n<li>Winner Certificates.<\/li>\n<li>Participation Certificates for all participants.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Rules &amp; Guidelines:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Participants must carry a valid college\/student ID card.<\/li>\n<li>Mobile phones, calculators, smart watches, books, notes, or any electronic devices are strictly prohibited.<\/li>\n<li>Participants must report at least 15 minutes before the event begins.<\/li>\n<li>Any attempt to violate the competition rules may result in immediate disqualification.<\/li>\n<li>The decision of the judges shall be final and binding.<\/li>\n<li>The organizers reserve the right to modify the rules, schedule, or any aspect of the event in the best interest of the competition with prior notice.<\/li>\n<li>Participants are advised to stay updated through official notices released by the organizing committee.<\/li>\n<li>Further modifications to the problem statement or event structure may be made if required.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Accommodation and Meals:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>Registration for the techFEST&rsquo;26 package is compulsory for accommodation and other perks, while participation in individual events is free*.<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>Registration &amp; Participation:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Registration starts on <strong>03 September, 2026<\/strong> and ends on <strong>25 September, 2026<\/strong>.<\/p>\n<p>Registered participants must be present at the venue on the scheduled date and time to take part in the competition.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Important Note:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Judge's decisions will be final and binding.<\/li>\n<li>Participants must report at least 15 minutes before the event starts. &nbsp;&nbsp;<\/li>\n<li>Any attempt to violate the competition rules may result in immediate disqualification.<\/li>\n<li>The organizers reserve the right to modify the rules, schedule, or any&nbsp;aspect of the event, with prior notice, in the best interest of thecompetition.&nbsp;<\/li>\n<li>All Participants are advised to stay updated through official notices&nbsp;released by the organizing committee on the SLIET techFEST 2026website (<a class=\"decorated-link\" href=\"https:\/\/www.techfest26.com\/\" target=\"_new\" rel=\"noopener\">https:\/\/www.techfest26.com\/package<\/a>)<\/li>\n<li>Further modifications to the problem statement may be made based on subsequent analysis and requirements.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>For Further Query:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>Domain Advisor:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Raju Kumar&nbsp;<\/li>\n<li>2341023\/GCS&nbsp;<\/li>\n<li>Contact: <strong>+91 6209681064<\/strong><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Domain Coordinator:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Aisha Kumari&nbsp;<\/li>\n<li>2442003\/GCT&nbsp;<\/li>\n<li>Contact: <strong>+91 6209681064<\/strong><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Event Coordinator <\/strong>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Jyotiraditya Bharadwaj<\/li>\n<li>254074001\/GME&nbsp;<\/li>\n<li>Contact: <strong>+91 9954441815<\/strong><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>For Non-SLIET Participants Only,<\/p>\n<p>techFEST 2026 is North India's premier technical festival. This is a paid opportunity with the packages mentioned below:<\/p>\n<p>Select Your Registration Package<\/p>\n<p><strong>\u20b9299 Package(Without Accommodation)<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Participation in all technical &amp; non-technical events<\/li>\n<li>Free entry to the Grand Cultural Evening<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>\u20b9599 Package(With Accommodation)<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Everything included in the \u20b9299 package<\/li>\n<li>Free accommodation for 2 days on campus(Extra Meal charges @50\/Diet)\u2028<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Note:&nbsp;<\/strong>Meal charges will be applicable as per institute norms<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Registration is mandatory for participation.<\/li>\n<li>Fee once paid is non-refundable.<\/li>\n<\/ul>","overall_prizes":"Exciting Prizes for Top 3 winners and participation certificates for all participants.","regn_open":1,"regn_type":1,"regn_url":null,"regn_email":null,"registration_clicks":0,"user_id":27463276,"moderation_status":1,"overall_leaderboard":0,"reject_reason":null,"display_date":null,"created_at":"2026-08-26T23:12:34+05:30","updated_at":"2026-10-04T23:55:30+05:30","communication_sent":null,"certificate_at":null,"remarks":null,"branding":0,"disable_auto_rounds":null,"certificate_config":null,"subtype":"","combined_leaderboard":null,"source":null,"short_id":"lj0byVW","hashtags":null,"participation_certificate":1,"winner_certificate_at":null,"listed":1,"self_moderated":2,"prizes_release_days":null,"checked":2,"display_title":null,"show_discussions_only_user":1,"show_reviews_only_user":1,"show_score_card":0,"players_count":177,"referral_leaderboard_show":0,"is_ad_free":0,"enable_gamify_leaderboard":0,"tpo_college_id":null,"publish_at":"2026-08-27 03:46:54","auto_shortlist_trigger":false,"enable_ai_discussion":false,"total_unlock_teams":0,"enable_hiring_automation":false,"auto_send_participation_certificate"